id: pm-stdin-schema-fields
title: Full-item stdin JSON must preserve declared schema and extension custom fields
description: "Disposable acceptance on 2026.10.9 confirms a declared schema string escape_class works through --escape-class but create --stdin-json converts it into --field key=escape_class,value=production_defect and refuses extension_item_field_unknown with provided_fields=[key]. Full-item JSON cannot represent project-defined schema fields despite accepting arbitrary metadata keys. Inspect schema-field versus registered-extension ownership before adapting custom values; retain typed refusal and typo guidance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-09T11:20:17.021Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-09T15:47:04.152Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-09T15:47:03.534Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-09T15:47:03.534Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Create and get-to-update stdin JSON round trips preserve declared string/number/boolean/object/array schema and extension fields; explicit flags retain precedence; undeclared fields and typos refuse before mutation; disposable CLI and public SDK tests prove exact item/history behavior.
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: The public SDK adapter resolves workspace metadata through declared option keys and aliases; CLI stdin supplies the selected schema. Raw extension assignments and per-field explicit overrides preserve scalar/container types. Persisted schema arrays retain their full shape.
expected_result: Declared schema and extension values survive create/get/update round trips; explicit flags win and invalid inputs preserve item and history bytes.
actual_result: "TDD keeper reproduced the defect before changes. Real temporary CLI and public SDK acceptance passed all five types, aliases and overrides; invalid/typo inputs preserved exact bytes. Linked tests, full 9966-test coverage at 100/100/100/100, static gates, manual acceptance and packed npm/Bun consumers passed."
