comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-09T11:20:17.021Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict complete 2908-item all-status corpus and request-specific stdin/custom-field search, open and in-progress inventories checked. Full live metadata and history read for closed pm-kipd, pm-qvdj, pm-2589e6 and pm-field-key-recovery. Those delivered full-item transport, extension setters, annotation integrity and rejected-key diagnostics; none owns this schema/extension custom-field transport defect. Reproduced with independent disposable tracker: init, schema add-field escape_class --type string --commands create,update,list,search,context, then stdin document versus explicit --escape-class. JSON stderr exit 2 names key; explicit create exits 0. This follow-up remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-09T11:25:22.007Z","harness:codex",Registered the completed full-item transport seed pm-kipd with the existing CLI/SDK/MCP contract-drift family so this recorded recurrence inherits mandatory static/coverage admission. Registration selects protections and does not assert the schema/extension transport defect is fixed. Item remains open and unclaimed.
  "2026-10-09T11:52:53.835Z","harness:codex","Graph admission: inspection of the already completed rejected-field diagnostic exposed that the stdin adapter supplies a generated key assignment instead of the actual schema field. Reuse its diagnostic lineage; the new transport defect remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-09T14:42:41.740Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: full live metadata, notes/learnings, history and closed transport/setter/recovery foundations inspected after strict 2912-item all-status intake with no omissions. Reproduce declared schema and extension fields, fix SDK-owned full-item adapter, retain explicit-flag precedence and refusal immutability. Deliver alongside cross-version workspace conformance in one PR; no new duplicate owner."
  "2026-10-09T14:58:57.902Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the existing adapter keeper failed before changes on malformed key-prefixed extension assignments and missing schema option mapping. The real disposable CLI keeper additionally reproduced persisted schema-array truncation: metadata arrays were interpreted as repeated flags. Scope includes distinguishing metadata containers from CLI occurrences, all five scalar/container types, aliases, per-field overrides, and byte-identical item/history after refusals. No overlapping test removed; unit grammar and real CLI/SDK persistence prove distinct boundaries."
  "2026-10-09T15:36:46.597Z","harness:codex",Linked sandbox-safe CLI/SDK keeper rerun passed after serialized build ownership. Full all-source suite passed 9966 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and no uncovered counts; no tests removed or coverage-ignore added. Strict lint and duplicate checks pass. New structured format refusal requires generated command and agent refusal inventories refreshed together; snapshots are regenerated through their canonical tools.
  "2026-10-09T15:46:23.502Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence: complete static quality pipeline passed without threshold changes, including lint, zero duplicate clones, docstring floors, package/SDK boundaries, generated snapshots, command/refusal/token budgets, tracker-context, graph composition, record integrity, import/transport cost checks and the existing mutation keeper. Focused linked transport tests and manual temporary tracker journey passed. Full-source coverage is exact 100/100/100/100, 9966 tests passing; public packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx consumers passed. Closure and generated changelog will be reviewed in the same implementation PR."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-09T15:13:52.184Z","harness:codex","Manual disposable CLI journey passed: schema add-field array with a distinct CLI flag and alias; Epic parent plus implements edge; stdin create; full get/edit/update with explicit alias override; undeclared-field refusal preserving exact item and history bytes; claim/start, evidence comment, close/release, and history hash verification plus storage/drift validation. Packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx smoke also passed for 2026.10.9 with nine first-party packages. Live observability: one-day Sentry critical/high counts zero, telemetry error rate 1.04 percent and missing-error-code rows zero; this is a pre-merge observation, not proof of post-merge trace freshness."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-09T15:08:42.179Z","harness:codex","Whole-item JSON is a transport contract, not CLI pair syntax: schema metadata keys must resolve through declared option identities; extension name=value assignments must preserve their raw payload; stored arrays must not be interpreted as repeated argv occurrences. Byte comparisons across both item and append-only history prove refusal atomicity."
